# 0150 WIP: MT6877 button driver (zero PMIC writes).
# Builds on 0149 v2.  Adds bsd/dev/ruby_keys.c behind rubkeys=1:
#   volume down  KPD KP_MEM1 bit 0 (0x10010000 + 0x04, clear while down)
#   volume up    MT6359 TOPSTATUS 0x2a bit 3 (HOMEKEY_DEB, clear while down)
#   power        MT6359 TOPSTATUS 0x2a bit 1 (PWRKEY_DEB, clear while down)
# TOPSTATUS is the PMIC's debounced key level and is independent of the PSC
# interrupt enable (0x910); the driver is read-only and writes no PMIC, rail,
# PSC status or KPD register.  The 0149 keywatcher never sampled 0x2a; the
# 2026-11-02 read-only check on 0149 v2 showed 0x2a bit3 toggling with volume
# up and bit1 with power while 0x910 stayed 0x0025.  0x198/0x916 read 0, so
# enabling 0x910 bit1 would expose an unhandled PMIC interrupt; it is dropped.
# The test cmdline is 0149 plus rubkeys=1 (sweethw=0, sweetgt=0, rubyprobe=1,
# rubypwrap=1, no rubypmic).  CI 41339839958 and image x16-0150-6c287707.img
# are recorded below; KERNEL_EXPECT_EXEC_DATA stays empty until the device run.
MACOS_VERSION=13.5
KERNEL_CONFIG=DEVELOPMENT
MACHINE_CONFIG=SWEET

BASE_REPO=https://github.com/MakrSas/ios-topaz.git
BASE_SHA=5095ac19dbdcf37b64b81fe443f4027ad51b84bf
